# Git identity & authorship (non-negotiable)

Every git action you perform — creating branches, committing, pushing, pulling,
opening or updating pull requests — MUST be attributed to the repository owner,
**Senuka Deneth**, and never to the Cursor agent. This applies identically in
Cloud Agents and local runs.

## Author identity

Before your first commit in any session, ensure the identity is set (local scope
so it never depends on the global Cursor default):

```bash
git config --local user.name  "Senuka Deneth"
git config --local user.email "113520257+Senuka-Deneth@users.noreply.github.com"
git config --local commit.gpgsign false
```

- Never commit or author as `Cursor Agent` / `cursoragent@cursor.com`.
- Never sign commits with the Cursor agent's SSH/GPG key. If the global config
  enables signing with a Cursor key, disable it locally (as above) so GitHub does
  not record a Cursor-owned signature.
- If the owner's email above is ever wrong, ask the owner rather than guessing.

## No "Cursor" footprint anywhere on GitHub

- **Never** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor ...`, `Co-authored-by: Cursor Agent ...`,
  or any Cursor/AI co-author trailer to a commit.
- **Never** add "Generated with Cursor", "Made by Cursor Agent", "🤖", or any
  similar attribution/notice to commit messages, PR titles, PR descriptions, or
  comments.
- Commit messages describe the change only. Do not reference the agent, the model,
  or the tooling that produced the change.
- Before pushing, verify no Cursor attribution remains:

```bash
git log --format='%an <%ae> | %cn <%ce> | %s' origin/main..HEAD
git log --format='%b' origin/main..HEAD | grep -i cursor   # must print nothing
```

If any commit is authored/committed by Cursor Agent or carries a Cursor trailer,
rewrite it (amend/rebase) to the owner identity and force-push the branch before
handing off.

> Note: the Cursor PR tool may append its own platform metadata footer to a PR
> body automatically; that is outside message content and cannot be removed from
> the body. Prefer integrating work by pushing to `dev` (see below) over tool-
> created PRs when a fully Cursor-free PR record is required.

## Branch policy for this project

- **Commit directly to the `dev` branch** for this repository. Do work on `dev`
  (or a short-lived branch that merges into `dev`), not against `main`.
- Do not push directly to `main`; `main` is updated by promoting `dev`.
